Origin and modifications
------------------------

INDRA was forked from goose at upstream version 1.50.0 (the version recorded in
[workspace.package] of Cargo.toml; the upstream repository recorded there is
https://github.com/aaif-goose/goose).

Files in this repository have been modified from their upstream form. As
required by Section 4(b) of the Apache License, the changes are:

  - Renaming of the project to INDRA across the shipped binary, crate names,
    environment variable prefixes (GOOSE_* to INDRA_*), and the user
    configuration directory. This rename is in progress; some upstream `goose`
    identifiers remain in the source tree.

  - Addition of a specialist routing layer under
    crates/indra/src/agents/specialists/, which classifies an incoming request
    into an operation and dispatches it to a domain specialist.

  - Removal of upstream project infrastructure that does not carry over to this
    fork, including the goose documentation site, blog, community channels, and
    organization automation.

  - Further modifications throughout the Rust crates and the Electron desktop
    application.

The goose name is used in this file and in the source tree only to identify the
upstream work from which INDRA is derived. This does not imply endorsement of
INDRA by Block, Inc., by AAIF, or by the goose maintainers.


